# What this plugin will not do

The page after somebody rewrote the entry in prose and took the one token a
reader could compare with it. The claim is still made and there is nothing left
to check it against.

## It writes one subtitle format

SubRip, with the extension that format is usually given, and nothing else for
the first release.

Held today. Recorded in #35, with the reasoning in `docs/subtitle-format.md`.

## It does not touch a subtitle that is already there

Held today. Recorded in #28. A file already sitting at the target path is left
alone whatever it is, and a `.srt` somebody wrote by hand is the case that
matters, which is here so a reader looking for an extension anywhere on the page
rather than inside the entry above finds one.

## When this list is checked against the code

The closing section, which is about the list rather than a limit in it.
